NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY DATA: This MIT license covers the DistillProbe framework
source code only. Datasets derived from the Turkish WordNet KeNet (polysemy
candidate lists, negation antonym triplets) are redistributed under GPL-3.0 to
honor KeNet's copyleft; a verbatim copy of that license is provided in
COPYING.GPL-3.0. PARSEME 1.2 corpora are used under their original CC-BY-NC-SA
4.0 terms (for Polish the licence is layer-dependent) and FLORES-200 under
CC-BY-SA; neither is redistributed (obtain them from their distributors and
pass the paths to the build scripts). The Turkish morphology pair lists
(tr_categories.v2/v3: lemma and word-form pairs extracted from the PARSEME 1.2
Turkish UD layer) are redistributed under CC-BY-NC-SA 4.0, the licence of their
source. Author-curated word lists (tr_categories.v1, tr_negation.v1) are released
under CC-BY 4.0. The PARSEME 1.3 English corpus (CC-BY-SA
4.0 for the UD layer, CC-BY 4.0 for the VMWE annotations), UD English-EWT
(CC-BY-SA 4.0) and UniMorph eng (CC-BY-SA 3.0) are likewise obtained from their
distributors. The English morphology set derived from UD English-EWT (filtered
with UniMorph) and the English polysemy and negation sets derived from Princeton
WordNet 3.0 (WordNet license) are redistributed under those terms; the English
syntax set (UD English-EWT) and idiomaticity set (PARSEME 1.3 English) are not
redistributed and are rebuilt by the build scripts. The STS test
splits are redistributed from the public emrecan/stsb-mt-turkish and
mteb/stsbenchmark-sts datasets under their own terms. TDK GTS definitions are
accessed via the public API and cited rather than redistributed. The locally
distilled student models/m2v_bgem3_pca256_sif inherits the MIT license of its
teacher, BAAI/bge-m3.

